    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48123" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thēŏdămas</span></b> ,
			antis, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θειοδάμας,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>king of the
			Dryopes</i>, <i>and father of Hylas</i>, <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">271</span></i>.
			— Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thēŏdă-mantēus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Theodamas</i>, <i>Theodamantean</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hylas,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the son of Theodamas</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					1, 20, 6</span></i>
			 (Thiodamanteus, Müll.).</div>
